@startuml
title Stage 2 - Implemented agent and interfaces

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
hide empty members

note as Scope
  Stage 2 implementation.
  Stage 1 renders stay in docs/Stage1-pdfs.
  A slash command or function key does not call the model.
  A sentence goes through AgentController.
end note

package "Interfaces" {
    interface UserInterface {
        + start(): void
    }
    class TerminalUI
    class MarketIntelFrame
    class DeskCommand
    class CommandParser
    class DashboardPanel
    class AgentPanel
}

package "Application" {
    class ApplicationContext {
        + createDefault(): ApplicationContext
    }
    class ResearchGateway {
        + execute(userId, action, arguments): ToolResult
        + explainMovement(userId, symbol): MovementReport
        + ask(userId, text): String
    }
    class SessionWorkspace {
        + login(username, password): User
        + addPosition(symbol, quantity, assetType): void
        + portfolio(): Portfolio
        + watchlist(): Watchlist
    }
}

package "Follow-up" {
    class AgentController {
        + handle(userId, input): String
        + noteLookup(userId, symbol, action): void
    }
    class RequestPlanner {
        + createPlan(input, previousSymbol): AgentPlan
    }
    class PromptBuilder
    class ResponseComposer {
        + compose(plan, result): String
        + composeMovement(plan, report): String
    }
    class AgentPlan
    class ConversationMemory {
        + lastSymbol(userId): String
        + remember(...): void
    }
}

package "Tools" {
    interface AgentTool {
        + supports(action): boolean
        + execute(request): ToolResult
    }
    class ToolManager {
        + registerTool(tool): void
        + execute(request): ToolResult
    }
    class MarketDataTool
    class ETFExposureTool
    class ComparisonTool
    class NewsTool
    class MarketMovementTool
    class MarketInsightTool
    class PortfolioAnalysisTool
}

package "Explanation" {
    class MarketExplanationService {
        + explain(context): String
    }
    interface LLMProvider {
        + generate(prompt): String
        + generateBrief(prompt): String
    }
    class GeminiLLMClient
}

UserInterface <|.. TerminalUI
MarketIntelFrame --> ResearchGateway
MarketIntelFrame --> DeskCommand
TerminalUI --> CommandParser
TerminalUI --> ResearchGateway
TerminalUI --> SessionWorkspace
DashboardPanel --> ResearchGateway
AgentPanel --> ResearchGateway

ApplicationContext --> ResearchGateway
ApplicationContext --> AgentController
ResearchGateway --> ToolManager
ResearchGateway --> AgentController
ResearchGateway --> MarketExplanationService
ResearchGateway --> SessionManager

AgentController --> RequestPlanner
AgentController --> ToolManager
AgentController --> ResponseComposer
AgentController --> ConversationMemory
AgentController --> MarketExplanationService
AgentController --> LLMProvider
RequestPlanner --> LLMProvider
RequestPlanner --> PromptBuilder
MarketExplanationService --> LLMProvider
LLMProvider <|.. GeminiLLMClient

ToolManager o-- AgentTool
AgentTool <|.. MarketDataTool
AgentTool <|.. ETFExposureTool
AgentTool <|.. ComparisonTool
AgentTool <|.. NewsTool
AgentTool <|.. MarketMovementTool
AgentTool <|.. MarketInsightTool
AgentTool <|.. PortfolioAnalysisTool

SessionWorkspace --> AuthService
SessionWorkspace --> PortfolioService
SessionWorkspace --> WatchlistService

note bottom of RequestPlanner
  Keyword plan always runs first.
  Gemini may return one allowlisted action.
  A disallowed action, bad JSON, or a
  stop-word ticker falls back to keywords.
  Portfolio add and remove are not allowlisted.
end note

note bottom of ResearchGateway
  Facade for both interfaces.
  execute() checks the session, runs one tool,
  and stores the symbol for a later pronoun.
  Portfolio edits go through SessionWorkspace,
  not through the model.
end note

@enduml
